              "question": "<p>Tardive dyskinesia is a condition that results in excessive or distorted facial movements like lip smacking and tongue thrusts, and can occur with long term use of (especially) the first generation (typical) antipsychotic agents due to dysregulation of the basal ganglia. </p>\n"
